<article class="env-lemma" id="01JS">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01JS">Lemma <span data-tag="01JS">26.17.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ and $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes with the same target. Let $S = \bigcup U_ i$ be any affine open covering of $S$. For each $i \in I$, let $f^{-1}(U_ i) = \bigcup _{j \in J_ i} V_ j$ be an affine open covering of $f^{-1}(U_ i)$ and let $g^{-1}(U_ i) = \bigcup _{k \in K_ i} W_ k$ be an affine open covering of $g^{-1}(U_ i)$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X \times _ S Y = \bigcup \nolimits _{i \in I} \bigcup \nolimits _{j \in J_ i, \  k \in K_ i} V_ j \times _{U_ i} W_ k  \]
</div>
  <p> is an affine open covering of $X \times _ S Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See discussion above the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>